145
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,180
You've got a president, a
vice president number 1,

146
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,360
vice president number 2.

147
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:29,090
So if order matters,
you use permutations.

148
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:32,650
That's the way to remember that,
PP, Permutation Presidency.

149
00:06:32,650 --> 00:06:34,835
Combination is similar,
but order does not matter.

150
00:06:34,835 --> 00:06:35,960
So that's like a committee.

151
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:38,377
If you have 10 people and you
need to take those 10 people

152
00:06:38,377 --> 00:06:41,200
and then, out of them, create
a committee of three people,

153
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,230
order doesn't matter.

154
00:06:42,230 --> 00:06:43,355
You would use combinations.

155
00:06:43,355 --> 00:06:44,980
Well, here what I'm
going to go through

156
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:47,210
is I'm going to look for
all the paths from one node

157
00:06:47,210 --> 00:06:48,540
to another node.

158
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:51,780
And since it's a directed
graph, order does matter.

159
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:53,810
So I want to use
permutations where--

160
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:55,260
